ADDITIONAL NOTE — DECISION-SUPPORT TOOL DISCLAIMER

This software (Silence Tax Optimizer, https://silence-tax.com) is a calibrated
theoretical simulation, not a forecasting instrument. Cost estimates are
order-of-magnitude scenarios within a 5–40% of revenue credibility band
conditional on the calibration assumptions documented in `autoreferat.md`
Aneks A. The model is NOT validated against firm-level cost data and SHOULD
NOT be used as the sole basis for material business decisions.

By using this software you acknowledge that:
1. The output is illustrative, not a substitute for an audit or due diligence;
2. Real-world organizational outcomes may differ substantially from model
   predictions, particularly outside the Polish (Hofstede PD=68, UA=93)
   cultural context the model was calibrated on;
3. The author makes no warranty about the suitability of the model for any
   specific organization, sector, or decision;
4. Material investment decisions (>500K PLN per the model's own guidance)
   should be preceded by a controlled pilot validating model assumptions
   against the user's firm-specific data.

The author retains the right to be cited under standard academic conventions
when this software, model, or formulas are used in research or commercial
analysis. Suggested citation:

  Mamcarz, P. (2026). Silence Tax Optimizer (Version YYYY.WW.B.P) [Computer
  software]. https://silence-tax.com. ORCID: 0009-0002-3274-4226.

For research collaboration or licensing questions outside MIT scope, contact
pawel@mamcarz.com.
